UID:10009171-1794943800-1794951000@sebastopolcalendar.com
SUMMARY:Lecture Two | The Social Sculpture - How Art Can Shape Society
DESCRIPTION:As part of the 2-week art exhibition\, STIMULANT: Art as Remedy for Diseased Culture\, Apocalypse Studio presents the 2nd lecture in their series. \nThe studio’s founder\, Apoc\, spent many years working with leaders in twenty countries on some of humanity’s toughest social challenges\, from war and poverty to the destruction of nature\, drug abuse\, immigration\, and violence. He will share his insights from these years\, focusing on why only the domain of culture can rebalance systemic breakdown and social decay. Apoc will introduce what he calls the “8th great art”\, Social Sculpture\, to add to the 7 already known (Painting\, Sculpture\, Literature\, Architecture\, Theater\, Film\, and Music). Social Sculpture is the art form of artfully co-creating society actively and together.
URL:https://sebastopolcalendar.com/event/lecture-two-the-social-sculpture-how-art-can-shape-society/
LOCATION:Laguna Lab\, 117 Morris St\, Sebastopol\, 95472
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://sebastopolcalendar.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/lecture-2-nov17-1200x800-1.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Apocalypse Studio":MAILTO:song@apocalypse.art
END:VEVENT
